<title>CANADA: Canadian West Coast Vessel Loadings - CWB.</title>
<headline>Canadian West Coast Vessel Loadings - CWB.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Wheat Board reported seven vessels cleared, five were loading, 10 waiting and 10 were due at the Canadian West Coast, as of Monday.</p>
<p>The longest wait to load on the West Coast was one day. One ship loaded in Churchill, one more was due. Four ships loaded in Thunder Bay, two waited and seven were due. Two ships loaded on the East Coast, four waited and seven more were due.</p>
<p>    Port	 Loading	Waiting</p>
<p>    Vancouver	 5	     8</p>
<p>    Prince Rupert   0	     2</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
